sub: expose how far ahead a renderer may ask for subtitles

vo_mediacodec pre-renders the OSD for the frame its cadence predicts next,
which means calling osd_render() for a pts the playloop has not reached.
That is only correct once every subtitle packet up to that pts is in the
decoder and no ordered-chapter segment switch lies before it: sd_ass renders
what it has, and sub_get_bitmaps() performs a pending segment switch as a
side effect of being asked for a later pts.

dec_sub now records, each time sub_read_packets() drains its stream, the
demuxer's buffered-range end at that moment: the demuxer reads interleaved
files sequentially, so every subtitle packet up to that position has been
handed to the decoder (or queued for the render in flight, which applies
them before it returns). sub_get_render_horizon() reports that position in
video time, capped at a pending segment start, INFINITY after demuxer EOF
and MP_NOPTS_VALUE before anything was read; osd_get_sub_render_horizon()
takes the minimum over the active subtitle objects, NAN when one is unknown.

A refresh seek after a track switch clears every queue and refills them
from the refresh point, so the bound stays valid while a newly enabled
track catches up. Sparse tracks are the reason the demuxer position is used
rather than the last subtitle packet: with a minute between two events the
latter would forbid pre-rendering for that whole minute.

